{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"zincous-activated-ant","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Operator directive (verbatim, 2026-08-13)\n'Update our contribution flow to note that Gerrit changes that have known issues like these should be marked as \"work in progress\" to avoid erroneous submission.'\n\n## Incident this encodes\nDuring a fleet pause, change 1727's revision f34549d099 carried five known review defects (including a silent compaction-suppression bug). The hold was recorded in ticket comments and a session log — and a peer session, following the standing both-+1s-submit rule, submitted it anyway (merged as d2dea317ec; fixed forward by 8fd5166a7b). A recorded-but-unenforced hold is invisible to other sessions; Gerrit's own WIP state is enforceable — a WIP change cannot be submitted.\n\n## Work\n- CONTRIBUTING.md (the canonical Gerrit recipe): add to the push/iterate section — when a pushed change has known unresolved issues (review findings being folded in, a defect found post-push, a deliberate hold), mark it WIP immediately: 'git push gerrit HEAD:refs/for/main%wip' at push time, or POST /a/changes/<n>/wip on an existing change; unmark with %ready / /ready when resolved. State the rationale: comments and tickets are advisory; WIP is the only hold every submitter (human, bot, or another agent session) is forced to respect.\n- The packaged code-review guide (src/rebar/_guides/passing-code-review.md, surfaced by 'rebar explain review'): mirror the rule in the iterate-on-findings section.\n- AGENTS.md Gerrit section: one lean line pointing at the rule (respect the file's pointer style).\n- Cross-link, one authoritative wording.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] CONTRIBUTING.md documents the WIP hold (both the push-time %wip form and the REST toggle) with the rationale, in the Gerrit iterate section.\n- [ ] rebar explain review surfaces the same rule (guide source updated; any packaging test/generator green).\n- [ ] AGENTS.md carries a one-line pointer.\n- [ ] Wordings cross-link rather than duplicate.","id":"e30d-b5e7-f4de-4f91","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Contribution flow: mark known-issue changes WIP in Gerrit"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786644849338470001,"uuid":"a8ffefd4-ac58-4aa8-aaec-32650e95813e"}